>> B2: Describe how file descriptors are associated with open files.
>> Are file descriptors unique within the entire OS or just within a
>> single process?

Descriptors are unique within a single process.  Each thread keeps a
list of fd_entry nodes; fd_alloc () gives the next number (0 and 1 are
the console), fd_lookup () scans the list, fd_close () and
fd_close_all () free the nodes.  A new thread starts with an empty
list, so descriptors are not inherited.  A list was chosen over a
fixed array to keep struct thread small (+12 bytes instead of +512)
and to avoid an arbitrary descriptor limit.

